<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-MAS starts Adelaide-Tokyo flights.</title>
<headline>RTRS-MAS starts Adelaide-Tokyo flights.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian Airline System Bhd has introduced a weekly direct same-plane service from Adelaide to Japan, with a total transit time of under 24 hours, the South Australian government said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Transport Minister Diana Laidlaw said the direct link would be a major benefit for exporters of perishable goods, particularly to Japan's lucrative seafood market.</p>
<p>The flight would leave Adelaide every Thursday and travel via Melbourne to Kuala Lumpur and on to Tokyo via Penang, she said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
